# subdoc = 3.5
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Whence some say that plays are called 'dramata' (that is, actions) because they imitate active performers. For this reason the Dorians lay claim to both Tragedy and Comedy—Comedy being claimed by the Megarians (both those here under their democracy and those from Sicily, for Epicharmus was a poet from there, long before Chionides and Magnes) and Tragedy by certain Dorians in the Peloponnese—making these names their own.
# literal_translation = Whence also dramas (that is actions) to be called themselves certain-ones say because imitate performing-ones. On account of which also claim tragedy-and and comedy Dorians (comedy indeed for Megarians and who here as in that which among themselves democracy made, and who out of Sicily; thence for was Epicharmus poet much prior being than-Chionides and Magnes, and tragedy certain-ones of-them who in Peloponnese) making names.
