# prose_translation = Just as Homer was preeminently the poet of serious subjects (for he alone composed imitations that were not only good but dramatic), so too he was the first to outline the forms of comedy, dramatizing not invective but the laughable; for his *Margites* bears the same relation to comedies as the *Iliad* and *Odyssey* do to tragedies.
