# sentence_id = 41
# document_id = 0086-034-lat
# subdoc = 4.13
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = But when tragedy and comedy appeared, those who gravitated toward either branch of poetry according to their natural bent became comic poets instead of iambic poets, or tragic teachers instead of epic poets, because these forms were greater and more honorable than those. Whether tragedy has now developed sufficiently in its forms or not—both judged in itself and in relation to the theater—is another question.
# literal_translation = Besides appearance moreover tragedy and comedy who to either poetry impelled according-to own nature, these indeed for iambs comic-poets made were, these however for verses of-tragedy doctors, on-account-of greater and more-honorable to-be forms these than-those. Superintend indeed therefore if has now tragedy species sufficiently or not, both itself according-to self judged to-be and to theaters, other reason.
