# sentence_id = 42
# document_id = 0086-034-lat
# subdoc = 4.14
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Having originated at first from improvisations (both tragedy itself and comedy, the former from those who led off the dithyramb, the latter from those who led off the phallic songs which even now remain established by law in many cities), both grew gradually, as creators advanced whatever was clear of it.
# literal_translation = Made therefore from principle improvisational (that is unformed) both itself and comedy, and this indeed from inchoating dithyramb, this however from these which phallic (that is vitious), which hitherto and now in many of-cities remain by-law statuted, little-by-little augmented are, producing as-much-as was manifest of-itself.
