# sentence_id = 71
# document_id = 0086-034-lat
# subdoc = 6.12
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = But the greatest of these is the structure of events; for tragedy is an imitation not of human beings, but of action, of life, and of happiness; and unhappiness lies in action, and the end is a certain action, not a quality. People are of a certain quality according to character, but happy or the opposite according to actions.
# literal_translation = Greatest moreover of-these is of-things consistency; tragedy for imitation is not of-men but of-action and of-life and of-happiness; and unhappiness in action is, and end action certain is, not quality. Are moreover according-to characters indeed of-what-sort certain, according-to actions moreover happy or contrary.
