# sentence_id = 101
# document_id = 0086-034-lat
# subdoc = 8.2
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = So too there are many actions of a single person, out of which no single action is formed. On this account, all those poets seem to err who have composed an *Heracleid*, a *Theseid*, and similar poems; for they think that since Heracles was one person, it is fitting for the plot to be one as well.
# literal_translation = Thus moreover also actions of-one many are, out-of which one no-one becomes action. On-account-of which all seem to-err whosoever of-poets Heracleid, Theseid and such poems poetized; they-think for, since one was Heracles, one and plot to-be to-agree.
