# prose_translation = There remains, then, the person intermediate between these. Such is the man who is neither preeminent in virtue and justice, nor falls into bad fortune through vice and wickedness, but through some error (hamartia), being one of those who enjoy great renown and prosperity, like Oedipus and Thyestes, and illustrious men from such families.
