# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = A well-constructed plot, then, must be single rather than double, as some claim, and must change not into good fortune from bad, but on the contrary from good fortune into bad, not on account of wickedness, but on account of a great error, either of a man such as has been described or of one better rather than worse.
# literal_translation = Necessary therefore well having plot single magis to-be than double, as-if certain say, and to-be-transformed non into good-fortune out-of ill-fortune, but contrary out-of good-fortune into ill-fortune, non on-account-of pestilence but on-account-of error great or of-what-sort said is or of-better magis or of-worse.
