# prose_translation = A conjunction is a non-significant sound that neither hinders nor produces a single significant sound out of multiple sounds, naturally positioned both at the extremes and in the middle, which it is not fitting to place at the beginning of an utterance by itself, like "quidem", "vel", "autem"; or a non-significant sound that is capable of making one significant sound out of multiple sounds.
