# prose_translation = Inflection (case) belongs to a noun or a verb; this signifies 'of this' or 'to this' and all such relations, or expresses number, like 'men' or 'man', or indicates performance modes, like question or command; for 'did he walk?' or 'walk!' are inflections of a verb according to these forms.
# literal_translation = Case moreover is of-noun or of-verb, this indeed according-to 'of-this' or 'to-this' signifying and whatever such-things, this moreover according-to which to-one or to-many, for-instance 'men' or 'man', this moreover according-to dramatic-modes, for-instance according-to interrogation, command. For 'walked' or 'was-walking' cases of-verb according-to these species are.
