# subdoc = 22.14
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Again, Ariphrades mocked the tragedians because they use expressions that no one would use in ordinary speech, such as "domatibus ab" (from houses) instead of "ab domatibus", or "sethen" (from thee), "ego autem nin" (him), "Achille de" (from Achilles) instead of "de Achille", and all such phrases.
# literal_translation = Further moreover Ariphrades tragedians mocked, because which no-one certainly would-say in speech in-these they-use, for-instance "domatibus ab" but not 'ab domatibus' and that "sethen" (that-is from thee) and that "ego autem nin" (that-is him) and "Achille de" but not 'de Achille', and whatever other such-things.
