# sentence_id = 310
# document_id = 0086-034-lat
# subdoc = 23.7
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = For from the *Iliad* or *Odyssey* only one or two tragedies can be made from each, but from the *Cypria* many, and from the *Little Iliad* more than eight—such as *The Award of Arms*, *Philoctetes*, *Neoptolemus*, *Eurypylus*, *The Beggary*, *The Laconian Women*, *The Sack of Troy*, *The Sailing Away*, *Sinon*, and *The Trojan Women*.
# literal_translation = For out-of Iliad indeed and Odyssey one tragedy makes each-of-two or two alone, out-of Cypria moreover many and out-of Little Iliad plus than eight, for-instance Hoplon Krisis, Philoctetes, Neoptolemus, Eurypylus, Ptocheia, Lakena, Iliu Persis, and Apoplus, and Sinon and Proiades.
