# prose_translation = For the poet himself ought to speak in his own persona as little as possible; for when doing so he is not an imitator. Now other poets perform in their own person throughout, and imitate few things and rarely; but he, after a brief prelude, immediately introduces a man, a woman, or some other characterful figure—and not one lacking character, but possessing character.
