# sentence_id = 330
# document_id = 0086-034-lat
# subdoc = 24.20
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = and plots should not be constructed out of irrational parts, but preferably contain nothing irrational at all. If that is impossible, the irrational element should lie outside the plot itself (such as Oedipus not knowing how Laius died), and not within the drama (as in *Electra*, with those reporting the oracle, or in the *Mysians*, with the man who came speechless from Tegea to Mysia).
# literal_translation = speeches-and non to-consist out-of parts irrational, but most indeed none to-have irrational. If moreover non, outside plot-telling, as-if Oedipus non to-know how Iolaus dead is, but non in drama (that-is action), as-if in Electra who oracles announcing or in Mysians who without voice out-of land into Mysia coming.
