# sentence_id = 348
# document_id = 0086-034-lat
# subdoc = 25.15
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = As to whether a word or action is well or not well spoken or performed by anyone, one must examine it looking not only at the deed or word itself to see if it is noble or base, but also at the person acting or speaking, to whom, when, for whom, or for what purpose he did or said it—for instance, whether to bring about a greater good or to avert a greater evil.
# literal_translation = Concerning that moreover whether well or non well either said is by someone or acted is, non only to-be-considered to self which acted is or said looking, if noble or base, but and to acting-one or speaking-one to whom or when or to-whom or whose grace, for-instance if of-greater good, that it-become, or of-greater evil, that it-be-removed.
