# subdoc = 25.16
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Other objections must be resolved by looking at the diction: for instance, by dialect usage, as in "oureas indeed first" (where "oureas" may mean sentinels rather than mules); and regarding Dolon, "who was indeed bad of form," not having an ill-proportioned body, but an ugly face, for Cretans call a handsome face "euprosopon". And "mix it stronger" does not mean unmixed wine as for drunkards, but prepare it faster.
# literal_translation = Which moreover to diction looking behooves to-dissolve, for-instance dialect "oureas indeed first"; by-chance for non mules says but guards. And Dolon "as of-form indeed if was bad" non body unproportioned but face ugly; for eueides (that-is of-good form) Cretans 'euprosopon' (that-is of-good face) call. And that "more-fervently moreover was-mixing" non that non mixed, as of-wine eager-ones, but that faster.
