# sentence_id = 350
# document_id = 0086-034-lat
# subdoc = 25.17
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Other expressions are metaphorical, as: "all gods and men slept all night long"; while he simultaneously says: "and whenever he looked toward the Trojan plain, the noise of flutes and pipes"; for "all" is used metaphorically for "many", since "all" is a kind of many; and "alone unsharing" is metaphorical, for the best known is called "alone".
# literal_translation = This moreover according-to metaphor said is, for-instance «others indeed gods and men helmeted were-sleeping whole night»; at-same-time moreover says «or when plain Trojan saw, of-flutes of-pipes-and consonance»; for 'all' for 'much' according-to metaphor said is, for all much something; and this «alone moreover unsharing» according-to metaphor; which for most-known alone.
