# prose_translation = This happened regarding Icarius: for critics think he was Laconian, and therefore consider it incongruous that Telemachus did not meet him upon coming to Lacedaemon. But matters stand perhaps as the Cephallenians say: for they say Odysseus married among them, and that his father-in-law was Icadius, not Icarius. The problem is thus likely due to a mistaken assumption.
# literal_translation = This moreover suffered which around Icarius. They-think for himself Laconian to-be; inconvenient therefore non to-meet Telemachus to-himself into Lacedaemon coming. This moreover by-chance has as-if Cephallenians say; at himself for they-say Odysseus, and to-be Icadius but non Icarius. On-account-of error moreover problem probable is.
