# prose_translation = Such, then, is tragedy, as the earlier actors held regarding their successors: for Mynniscus called Callippides an ape because he went to great excesses, and a similar opinion was held of Pindar. As these actors stand to their successors, so the whole art of tragedy stands to epic.
